You are working in D:\Coding\Sannidhi (Next.js 15, Playwright e2e in ./e2e, Windows, pwsh, bun package manager). Task: add an automated axe-core accessibility scan to the e2e suite.

## Step 1
Run: `bun add -d @axe-core/playwright`

## Step 2
Edit e2e/a11y.spec.ts — add this import at the top (after the existing `@playwright/test` import):
```ts
import AxeBuilder from "@axe-core/playwright";
```
and append this test at the end of the file:
```ts
test("marketing and auth surfaces pass an axe serious/critical scan", async ({ page }) => {
  for (const path of ["/", "/login", "/request-access", "/signup"]) {
    await page.goto(path);
    const results = await new AxeBuilder({ page }).withTags(["wcag2a", "wcag2aa"]).analyze();
    const serious = results.violations.filter(
      (violation) => violation.impact === "critical" || violation.impact === "serious",
    );
    const summary = serious.map((violation) => `${violation.id}(${violation.impact})`).join(", ");
    expect(serious, `${path} axe violations: ${summary}`).toEqual([]);
  }
});
```

Do NOT modify the existing three tests in that file. Do NOT run the e2e suite (it requires a Convex backend that is not running). Do NOT touch any other files.

Report back: the exact version of @axe-core/playwright that got installed (read it from package.json), confirmation of the spec edit, and any anomalies.

